From: Sébastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] launch_proxy: do not require sudo to clear the stale pidfile

launch_proxy.sh runs under "set -e" and clears a stale proxy pidfile
with "sudo rm -f" before starting proxy_ara240. rt-sdk-ara2_script.sh
already refuses to run as anything but root, so the whole service runs
as root and sudo adds nothing -- but on an image that does not ship
sudo the command exits 127 and set -e terminates the script before the
proxy is ever launched.

Nothing reports the failure. rt-sdk-ara2_script.sh backgrounds this
script without checking its exit status and then logs success
unconditionally, so systemd records the unit as active (exited),
status=0/SUCCESS, with no proxy running and no socket at the
interface_socket_file path clients wait on.

Drop sudo and clear the pidfile directly.

Upstream-Status: Pending [reported to NXP]
Signed-off-by: Sébastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
---
 usr/share/rt-sdk-ara240_2.1.1/scripts/launch_proxy.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/usr/share/rt-sdk-ara240_2.1.1/scripts/launch_proxy.sh
+++ b/usr/share/rt-sdk-ara240_2.1.1/scripts/launch_proxy.sh
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 		log_message "Proxy is already running." "$PROXY_LOG_FILE"
 	else
 		log_message "Launching proxy..." "$PROXY_LOG_FILE"
-		sudo rm -f /var/run/dvproxy.pid
+		rm -f /var/run/dvproxy.pid
 		cd "$PROXY_DIR" || {
 			log_message "Error: Failed to navigate to proxy directory: $PROXY_DIR" "$PROXY_LOG_FILE"
 			exit 1
